-- title:
--   Inertia eigenvector of level-two tame type at p=3
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p = 3$; let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta(W) \neq 0$ which is a semistable model in the sense that every prime $q$ with $q \mid \Delta(W)$ satisfies $q \nmid c_4(W)$, and whose $p$-torsion over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and has no Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodule other than $0$ and itself. Let $N' \geq 1$ with $p \nmid N'$, and assume that either $5 \leq p$ or some prime $q \mid N'$ has $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$. Let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \in S_0$, let $k'$ be an integer with $2 \leq k' \leq p+1$, let $i \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $\mathfrak{m}'$ be a maximal ideal of the anaemic Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N' k' S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_{k'}(\Gamma_0(N'))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N'$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N'$, $q \notin S_0$, such that $p \in \mathfrak{m}'$ and such that for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta(W)$ one has $T_\ell - \ell^i a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}'$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$. Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\theta$ a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N' k' (S₀ \ {p})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $F$ whose composite with the inclusion of the algebra at level set $S_0$ has kernel $\mathfrak{m}'$ and which kills $T_p$. Let $kn \in \mathbb{N}$ with $kn = k'$, and let $\rho : \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ be a monoid homomorphism trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, such that for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$, $\ell \nmid \Delta(W)$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field, $\operatorname{tr} \rho(\sigma) = \theta(T_\ell)$ and $\det \rho(\sigma) = \ell^{kn-1}$. Finally let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ having $p$ as a nonunit, let $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfy $\pi^{p^2-1} = p$, and let $\psi_k : F \to \kappa(P)$ be a ring homomorphism into the residue field of $P$. Then there is a nonzero $v \in \kappa(P)^2$ such that, for all $\sigma$ in the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$, either $(\psi_k \rho(\sigma)) v = \varphi(\sigma)^{kn-1} v$ for all such $\sigma$, or $(\psi_k \rho(\sigma)) v = (\varphi(\sigma)^{p})^{kn-1} v$ for all such $\sigma$, where $\varphi(\sigma)$ denotes the residue of $\sigma(\pi)/\pi$ when that lies in $P$ and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the $p = 3$ instance of the representation-side form of the supersingular (level-two fundamental character) shape of inertia at $p$ for a mod-$p$ eigensystem with $a_p = 0$, in the tradition of Fontaine, Serre and Edixhoven, here stated with the determinant prescribed as the $(k-1)$-st power of the cyclotomic character on Frobenii. It feeds the weight comparison for the Frey curve at the prime $3$, being cited by the passage from a maximal ideal in weight $k'$ to one in weight $2$ or $p+1$.
